## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of provider aliases and per-environment module instantiation in Terraform.

## Key Concepts
- Provider aliases and module-level provider mappings
- For_each environment deployment and target verification
- Safe plan/apply separation per environment

## Code Example
```javascript
provider "aws" {
  alias = \"dev\"
  region = \"us-west-2\"
}
provider "aws" {
  alias = \"prod\"
  region = \"us-east-1\"
}
variable \"environments\" { type = \"map(string)\"; default = { prod = \"prod\"; staging = \"staging\" } }

module \"vpc\" {
  for_each = var.environments
  source   = \"./modules/vpc\"
  providers = {
    aws = each.key == \"prod\" ? aws.prod : aws.dev
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test rollback if prod plan uses the wrong alias?
- How can you enforce alias usage at plan time to prevent mix-ups?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests environment isolation via provider aliases and per-env backends, plus CI gating for safe promotion to QA.

## Key Concepts
- Provider alias isolation
- Backend per environment
- CI gated plan/apply workflow

## Code Example
```hcl
terraform {
  required_version = ">= 1.4"

  backend "s3" {
    key    = "envs/qa/terraform.tfstate"
    region = "us-west-2"
  }
}

provider "aws" {
  alias = "qa"
  region = "us-west-2"
  assume_role {
    role_arn = "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_QA:role/TerraformRole"
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle secrets across environments?
- What are trade-offs of provider alias vs separate workspaces?
